# Copy this to .env and fill in real values. .env must be gitignored.
#
# NOTE: unlike P0-06 (Zoho) and P0-07 (Dropbox), this spike uses NO OAuth.
# That is the point, not a shortcut — see README.md. IMAP with an
# app-specific password is the provider-agnostic path, and OAuth here would
# be Google-specific and would not transfer to a practice on Exchange.

# The IMAP endpoint. Gmail's values are the defaults below; a practice on
# another provider changes only these two lines, which is exactly the
# portability claim this spike is testing.
#   Gmail            imap.gmail.com          993
#   Outlook/M365     outlook.office365.com   993
#   Zoho Mail        imap.zoho.in            993
IMAP_HOST=imap.gmail.com
IMAP_PORT=993

# The shared inbox being monitored. Development/test account only —
# never the practice's real shared inbox.
IMAP_USER=work.caos@gmail.com

# App-specific password, NOT the account password. Requires 2FA to be
# enabled on the account first. Google shows it as four groups of four
# characters; spaces are stripped by the script, so paste it either way.
#
# This is a credential with full mailbox access. Same discipline as every
# other secret in this project: .env only, never committed, revoked from
# the Google account when the spike is finished.
IMAP_APP_PASSWORD=<app-specific-password>

# Mailbox to poll. "INBOX" is correct for a plain shared inbox; a practice
# routing mail into a label/folder would point this at that folder instead.
IMAP_MAILBOX=INBOX
